# Kena: Bridge of Spirits (PPSA01802), Linux/AMD: main menu -> New Game -> difficulty -> brightness -> first level load.
#
# Anchors are SECONDS from the first pad poll, held for 1 s each. On Linux the title polls the pad
# fast while it boots (pad read 54 arrives about 8 s in), so reach-first-gameplay-prompt.pad's
# pad-read anchors all fire about 40 s in, before the menu appears at about 200 s. Each 1 s hold
# below spans at least one menu read.
#
#   230 s  New Game on the main menu (the default selection)
#   262 s  Next on "Choose Difficulty" (default: Spirit Guide), seen on screen at pad flip 1000
#   300 s  Accept on the brightness calibration screen -> first level load
#   340 s+ a Cross every 25 s for the intro narration. The guest stops polling during the level
#          load, so the presses between about 300 s and 515 s are not read.
#
# Measured 2026-10-07 on Linux/RADV, prosper-app in a visible window, main 97917c5f (PROSPER_NULL_PAGE=1,
# PROSPER_GUEST_ARGS= empty, fresh save roots). The first level load then loses the Vulkan device in
# 2 of 2 runs, at about 500 s and 640 s (radv: "context is guilty of a hard recovery"). So this
# route has not yet been seen to reach gameplay. See prosper/docs/games/KENA_STATUS.md.
230+1.0:cross
262+1.0:cross
300+1.0:cross
340+1.0:cross
365+1.0:cross
390+1.0:cross
415+1.0:cross
440+1.0:cross
465+1.0:cross
490+1.0:cross
515+1.0:cross
540+1.0:cross
565+1.0:cross
590+1.0:cross
615+1.0:cross
640+1.0:cross
665+1.0:cross
690+1.0:cross
715+1.0:cross
740+1.0:cross
765+1.0:cross
